  "caveats": [
    "Pooled stratum AUROC (+0.0854) pools responses across all 10 subsets. The readout is ONE calibrated model so its scores are comparable across subsets; the frozen hard-max probabilities are NOT cross-subset calibrated. Part of the pooled gap is therefore calibration, not composition. The per-subset mean stratum delta (+0.0160) is the confound-free figure and is the one used against the registered +0.03 bar.",
    "The readout consumes the frozen per-window scalar (as a logit) alongside the CLS vector, so it can in principle recover max-like behaviour; it does not, and its per-subset profile is a genuine re-ranking rather than a smoothing of the max.",
    "Training-slice window sets are smaller than arena ones (mean 2.64, max 14 windows vs arena means of 3-23 and a long tail on techqa/expertqa). The readout is read out-of-distribution in set size on the two largest-evidence subsets.",
